// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/course/goldenfloat.t27 -- the t27 course on GoldenFloat: a family of floats split by phi
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which reads
; it the way it reads specs/course/ai-numbers.t27: the constant schema, every test block below,
; every widget in specs/widgets/gallery.t27, every lesson spec compiled clean, the Russian bundle
; named by specs/course/goldenfloat-ru.t27. It writes this course into src/lib/course.generated.ts
; (the page at #/goldenfloat) and a byte-identical copy of this file at public/learn/goldenfloat.t27.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN). The Russian words live in the bundle.

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 3 of specs/course/courses.t27, 27 modules of one lesson each, on the
; GoldenFloat family of arXiv:2606.05017. Modules 1 to 6 give the rule and the numbers behind it:
; E = round((N - 1) / phi^2), the Lucas identities, phi kept in 16 bits. Modules 7 to 23 walk the
; family rung by rung from GF4 to GF1024, with a dot product in GF-T16 after GF16. Modules 24 to 27
; put the exponent in trits (GF-T8, GF-T16, GF-T32) and count the decode steps.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it says no number of its own. Every lesson quotes only the
; constants and test values of the spec it opens, and arithmetic of them. No lesson claims a
; speed, an accuracy on a model or a result on hardware. Where a test writes its value in rather
; than computing it, the lesson says so.

; WHAT IS PENDING: 7 lessons (2, 4, 5, 9, 11, 15, 16) have their own spec in the repository, but it
; does not compile clean in the browser compiler yet. Each opens a placeholder widget that shows
; no run, and opens the family spec, numeric/goldenfloat_family.t27, until its own spec is clean.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module goldenfloat;

